domain CC304_WIP_HANDOFF:
  description "Bounded handoff, one WIP commit, and one verified branch push before interruption."

problem P1:
  |
    Preserve the exact resumable state of the accepted revision-8 planning,
    Seal-based test-authority implementation, retained revision-scope experiments,
    and the active cc304 controlled revise trial, without advancing product authority
    or losing the distinction between diagnostic and current evidence.

evidence E1:
  |
    The owner explicitly instructed Codex to interrupt here after creating handoff
    material, making one WIP commit, and pushing it. The established interpretation
    of that instruction is an exact restart point and limits, one intended WIP commit,
    one push, remote-SHA readback, and then stop.

evidence E2:
  |
    After a canonical secdat-routed fetch, local HEAD and
    origin/codex/compact-psyche-repair-integration both resolve to
    475ff90a5a7ac42645d2ccdd7f02d9f8f8fda23c with ahead and behind counts zero.
    The linked worktree is the matching active worktree and the main checkout
    /home/katsumata-m/kshiai owns the repository secdat domain.

evidence E3:
  |
    The dirty worktree contains the accepted ADR-0034 test-authority selector and
    Seals, accepted plan revision 8 and PERT transition, preserved unsealed
    revision-scope/Ollama experiments, and the cc304 controlled appearance-revise
    implementation, diagnostic test, exact draft/stale Seals, and evidence records.
    These changes share the same decision history and must remain visibly WIP.

evidence E4:
  |
    The final local checks report current-authority npm tests passing, typecheck
    passing, PERT document check passing with pre-existing warnings, SealGraph fsck
    result ok, and the cc304 decision audit with no fatal, error, or warning. The
    focused-authoring file separately passed 7 diagnostic tests but its verification
    Seal is STALE_TRANSITIVE and the selector correctly excludes it from current
    evidence.

evidence E5:
  |
    No paid provider call, deployment, policy activation, final acceptance, merge,
    release, production mutation, current-character pointer movement, or workday-end
    record is part of the preserved WIP. Ignored secrets, environment files, database
    data, generated dist output, and user media are not listed as tracked changes.

premise SCOPE:
  |
    The WIP commit may preserve all repository changes already present in this
    dedicated task worktree plus the exact handoff record. It must not rewrite,
    discard, rebase, merge, activate, accept, or reinterpret any preserved artifact.

premise REMOTE_WRITE:
  |
    Push exactly the resulting local branch tip to the existing same-named remote
    branch through the verified secdat route. Do not retry an ambiguous push. Read
    the remote ref back independently and require it to equal the local commit.

pending U1:
  |
    The final WIP commit SHA is determined only after the handoff file is staged and
    committed. The handoff can identify the restart point as the branch tip containing
    itself; the exact SHA belongs in the post-commit and remote readback report.

decision D1 based_on P1, E1, E2, E3, E4, E5, SCOPE, REMOTE_WRITE, U1:
  |
    Create one complete Japanese handoff that records the pre-WIP base, preserved
    change groups, validations, exact Seal limitations, unperformed actions, and
    restart gate. Review the full staged inventory, create one sentence-case WIP
    commit, push the current branch once to its existing remote branch, read back the
    remote SHA, and then perform no further repository work.
